# The tools a local wine profile carries, read by scripts/wine-env.sh.
#
# One place for the versions, so a bump touches this file and nothing else. Plain KEY=value
# lines: the script sources this file, so it must stay free of anything but assignments.
#
# Every archive is checked against its SHA256 before it is unpacked. The two sums below were
# compared with what each publisher states, on 2026-11-02:
#   PortableGit: the `digest` GitHub shows for the release asset (sha256).
#   Python:      `packageHash` in the NuGet registration for python 3.12.8 (SHA512, base64);
#                the SHA256 here is of the same file.
# A changed sum means the download is not the file this manifest was written for. Do not edit
# the sum to make it pass: find out why it changed.
#
# Changing any line changes the profile's key, so the next `wine-env.sh setup` builds a new
# profile beside the old one instead of mutating it.

# PortableGit: a 7z self-extracting archive, so `7z x` unpacks it on Linux with no installer.
# It gives the profile bash.exe (CODESCOUT_BASH) and git.exe (WINEPATH).
PORTABLEGIT_VERSION=2.55.0.5
PORTABLEGIT_URL=https://github.com/git-for-windows/git/releases/download/v2.55.0.windows.5/PortableGit-2.55.0.5-64-bit.7z.exe
PORTABLEGIT_SHA256=5aa8a20f6e9abb2c755f0e73c91c687701a46b309ad84a0ca6509380fa4ae290

# CPython from the NuGet `python` package: a full layout (DLLs, Lib), unpacked with `7z x`, no
# installer. NOT the "embeddable" zip from python.org: that one ships `python312._pth`, which
# makes the interpreter ignore PYTHONPATH and the script's own directory, so two
# `run_command::attribution` tests fail under it (measured 2026-11-02). Under this package all
# 28 attribution tests and the 3 `librarian::requirements` hook tests pass.
PYTHON_VERSION=3.12.8
PYTHON_URL=https://www.nuget.org/api/v2/package/python/3.12.8
PYTHON_SHA256=406856be971d957e0bee7a5cefe20a5ec78d70a495e9e33cd0e53d31faec049d
